BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bobby McFerrin's MOTION
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260605T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260605T203000
UID:260528bPJoaUk2ukOJyYGaIPg3RQ
DESCRIPTION:**In 2021\, Bobby McFerrin asked David Worm to bring together 
 singers to play and improvise together. The result is MOTION\, a collectiv
 e of masterful vocalists and facilitators dedicated to the transformationa
 l potential of improvised sound. Bryan Dyer\, David Worm\, and Destani Wol
 f have joined Bobby on stage and in the studio\, creating songs in the mom
 ent\, facilitating Circlesinging\, harmonizing and connecting their intuit
 ive voices weekly for 4 years as the band MOTION. They continue to perform
  and create vocal community space to honor healing and peace\, every Monda
 y at The Freight in Berkeley.**\n\nThe Bay Area has been washed in the pow
 erful and heart felt vocals of each member of acapella band MOTION since t
 hey started their musical journeys in their hometowns of Berkeley\, Oaklan
 d\, and Los Altos Hills. Bryan Dyer\, David Worm\, and Destani Wolf’s in
 dividual paths have taken them around the globe\, recording and performing
  with the best. From **Quincy Jones\, Michael McDonald\, Ladysmith Black
  Mambazo\, The Pharcyde\, John Cale\,** on Grammy nominated albums to vo
 cal collaborations with multidisciplinary arts such as **Cirque du Soleil
 \, Robert Moses Kin\, Bandaloop\, Tandy Beal and Axis Dance**. Besides the
 ir voices and compositions being including in TV and film (Disney’s “T
 he Descendants”\, HBO’s “Momentum Generation”\, “Set up” Benja
 min Bratt’s “The Mission”\, Kevin Harts: “Laugh at my Pain”\, FO
 X’s “SYTYCD” and more) they are veteran acapella vocalists dedicated
  to using their voices to empower and inspire hope and create positive cha
 nge in their communities and worldwide. \n\nMOTION shares a collective vi
 sion of music and the voice healing ourselves and the world. They have tau
 ght vocal technique\, improv\, circle singing at world renowned learning i
 nstitutes like Omega Institute in New York\, The Esalen Institute in Big S
 ur California\, The Berkeley School of Music\, San Francisco Music Conserv
 atory\, UCLA\, Living Jazz\, to name a few. Together they are enlightened 
 and inspired by performing and facilitated classes and workshops in the ho
 pes of illuminating open heart’s and building community through song.\n\
 nFriday\, June 5th\, at 8:30pm. Admission is free!
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/motion/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
