SUMMARY:Live Music Saturday
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T200000
UID:260519CFZR85R-ukGaOB_UwGc30g
DESCRIPTION:Tori Roze & Johnny Alexander This is Soul for today: tight\, s
 ophisticated\, and up-to-date...a winner" \\(San Diego Troubadour\\). Tori
  Roze and Johnny Alexander are two members of a larger six piece original 
 funky soul-jazz band called Tori Roze and The Hot Mess from San Diego\, CA
 . The band\, of which Alexander and Roze are the primary songwriters\, has
  been nominated for seven San Diego Music Awards including "Best Acoustic 
 Performer\," "Best Blues Album\," and "Best Pop Album." Tori funnels her m
 usical influence down from childhood favorites Michael Jackson\, Erykah Ba
 du\, Ella Fitzgerald\, Bjork\, Whitney Houston\, and musical theatre - bri
 nging forth a uniquely syncopated\, clever\, interesting\, and unmatched b
 lending of audio tapestries. Alexander\, a diverse man of music ranging fr
 om The Smiths to jazz and classic rock\, is a sound magician inverting sta
 ndard chord structures and time signatures into beautiful landscapes\; his
  contributions are full of brilliant luminescence. As musical atmospheric 
 chameleons\, their desire is to bring forth a deeply emotionally-connected
  performance to every audience who has the pleasure of seeing them. Tori R
 oze & The Hot Mess · Collabs
LOCATION:Ferry Taproom
URL:https://www.mareislandbrewingco.com/events/live-music-saturday-0606202
 6
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Summertime Livin' Easy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T180000
UID:260519BJoOUOaETkOwtNM91fQRNQ
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  5/15/26\n\n**JUNE EXHIBIT: SUMME
 RTIME LIVIN’ EASY**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  **June 1 – June 28\, 2026**\n\
 n**RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, June 6\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Nancy Gra
 y  and Gallery artists\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show a
 nd the Gallery’s 29th anniversary.  Be sure to take part in the Gallery
 ’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work by a Gallery artist.  Re
 freshments will feature the Gallery’s signature mocktail: Brushstroke Fi
 zz.**\n\nSonoma County artist\, **Nancy Gray\,** unveils new summer-inspir
 ed acrylic paintings that are a colorful expressive interpretation of the 
 region’s beauty.  Summer is the artist’s favorite season and it shows
 . Drawing inspiration from the French Fauvist tradition\, these works abou
 nd with interpretive color choices and bold brush work.  Non-literal colo
 r expression plays out in “Evening Shade” as backlit trees cast blue t
 endrils of shade dancing on a bed of reddish ground.  Sprinkled across a 
 carpet of golden yellow\, vibrant red poppies glow in “Sundrenched Splen
 dor\,”amplifying the heat of the midday sun.  Red poppies take on a dra
 matic contrasting role in “Lavender Fields Forever” as they play again
 st the purplish blues and lavenders of the fields and sky.  Inspired by t
 he landscape\, these works reinterpret it through emotion and memory.  
 “We are blessed to live amongst Sonoma’s breathtaking scenery – ever
 ywhere I look\, I see a painting\,” noted Gray.\n\nGray has had a lifelo
 ng passion for art.  A Texas native\, she loves living in wine country wi
 th its inspirational landscapes.  Along with the Fauvist painters\, early
  years vacationing on the Caribbean Coast and Belize influenced her bright
  color palette.  She began exhibiting her art in Houston in the early 90
 ’s and continued to focus on her painting after moving to Sonoma County.
   Gray exhibits regionally and has been a member of the Upstairs Art Gall
 ery for five years.\n\nMeet the artist: Gray will host the Gallery on June
  18 and 25 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features
  **Collective Expressions: 29 Years\,** a members’ collaborative show ce
 lebrating the Gallery’s 29th anniversary. Gallery artists offer an excit
 ing mix of mediums\, subject matter and styles emblematic of the Gallery
 ’s dynamic diversity.  Landscapes by Barretta\, Laland\, and Zorich hig
 hlight our region’s beauty\; travel afar with Bird’s Paris cityscape\;
  from sunflowers to roses\, flowers star in works by Gray\, Haley\, Miller
 \, Schaffer\, Sumner and Wilson\; succulent oranges are the focus of Stolp
 er’s stunning still-life\; lovable pets are the subject of Tobin-Charles
 ton’s jewelry\; abstracts by Morgan and Reid bring a moving contemporary
  complement\; figurative works by Rapp\, Roney and Shore round out this cl
 assic to contemporary overview of the Upstairs artistic family.\n\nAlso jo
 in us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, June 4\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART 
 NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community ev
 ent celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participating. 
  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Hea
 ldsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **ww
 w.upstairsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly 
 Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:“Brush with Nature” plein air art event
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T150000
UID:260514ZC3BKKLlxECnyC45o3zJ-w
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a plein air painting event\, where art and nature 
 come together in real time. Talented plein air artists will be scattered t
 hroughout the park\, capturing its beauty on canvas. Pick up a map in Chin
 a Camp Village and set out to find the artists in the field\, and experien
 ce how they transform a vista into a work of art.\n\nThen return to the vi
 llage to view more beautiful plein air art—and maybe find something spec
 ial to take home—at a one-day silent auction. (A portion of the proceeds
  will go to Friends of China Camp.) Also at the village\, join an art clas
 s to try your own hand at plein air painting—no previous experience requ
 ired\, and we’ll provide all the supplies to get you started. Special ki
 ds’ painting classes will also be offered.  Whether you’re here to cr
 eate\, learn\, or simply be inspired\, you’ll have a chance to connect w
 ith art—and artists—in an unforgettable setting.\n\n**SCHEDULE OF EVEN
 TS**\n\n10 a.m. – 1 p.m. Plein air artists stationed throughout the park
  Free map available at China Camp Village Cafe\, Back Ranch Meadows Campgr
 ound kiosk\, and Turtle Back Trail parking area.\n\n10 a.m. – 3 p.m. Ple
 in air art sale (China Camp Village)\n\n11 a.m. Children’s plein air pai
 nting class for children ages 6 to 12 (China Camp Village)\\*\n\n1 p.m. Pl
 ein air painting class for adults (China Camp Village)\\*\n\n1 p.m. Plein 
 air painting class for children ages 6 to 12 (China Camp Village)\\*\n\n1 
 p.m. – 3 p.m. Meet artists (China Camp Village)\n\n*Self-guided walking 
 tour to visit plein aire artists in the field is open to all. Registration
  for aur classes is required. Cancellation notified via email.*\n\n**Date:
 ** Saturday\, June 6 **Time:** 10 a.m. – 3 p.m. (see below for class t
 imes and registration) **Location:** China Camp Village **Cost:** free to
  FOCC members\, $5 **donation** appreciated for non-members **Ages:** a
 ll ages welcome to event (see below for classes)\; under 18 must be accomp
 anied by a responsible adult
LOCATION:China Camp Village
URL:https://friendsofchinacamp.org/event/brush-with-nature-plein-air-event
 /
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
