BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Callie Watts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T000000
UID:260417vp9jGcy1vE27L7GCEX8Lbw
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:Lost Church Santa Rosa
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108212388?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Park Rx—Beginner Hiking for Fitness Spring 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T120000
UID:260413iTmsx-2_OU-_uZHUxBenhQ
DESCRIPTION:Join us on this fitness program\, where the leaders w
 ill guide you on a series of 8 weekly hikes with the challenge
  increasing each week. Before the first hike\, the leader will 
 discuss proper shoes\, hydration\, incorporating hiking poles\, pro
 per pacing\, etc. The group's final hike aims for the long rout
 e up Brushy Peaks Trail\, where hikers can enjoy the beautiful 
 vistas.\n\nThe series costs $80 (plus a $10 parking fee per visi
 t. Note that the Sugarloaf Annual Pass is $59 and valid at Sug
 arloaf and Jack London SHP)\, or free-of-cost for participants wi
 th a March 2026 or newer Park Rx from a Sonoma County Medical
  Provider. Click https://sugarloafpark.org/activities/parks-rx-program/
  for information on our Park Rx program and to download the fo
 rm. The number of **available Park Rx tickets is limited**\; **pl
 ease have your Rx ready at the time of sign up**.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/beghffspring26
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Big West Wine Fest
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T180000
UID:260412n5U0q9964EyzrQWthvPg4w
DESCRIPTION:Tickets are now on sale for Big West Wine Fest\, the largest g
 athering of California natural winemakers. The event takes place in the ic
 onic redwood grove at Solar Punk Farms just steps from downtown Guernevill
 e and the Russian River. \n\n“When Nina & I met we were working for lea
 ders in Sonoma County’s natural wine scene. We were inspired to celebrat
 e our local community outside of the typical wine festival structure. Our 
 intention is to capture an expansive sample of this moment in Northern Cal
 ifornia wine culture in a way that truly reflects this place. You can expe
 ct to taste wines from producers pouring their 40th vintage to producers r
 eleasing their first bottlings.” (Emily Weber\, Co-Founder). Check out t
 he full line up of over 75 producers from Sonoma County & further afield o
 nline at www.bigwestwinefest.com**.**
LOCATION:Solar Punk Farms
URL:http://bigwest.biz
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Where the Light Feels Like Home
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T170000
UID:260412bWTFTL-TLk-8OU_cWHfbAQ
DESCRIPTION:You are warmly invited to an exclusive exhibition of paintings
  by Sonoma -based artist and landscape designer Ann Rosmarin\, held in her
  home studio.\n\nOriginally from South Africa\, Ann draws inspiration from
  a life journey that brought her to California by way of London and the Mi
 dwest. Landscape and memory play a central role in her work\, which moves 
 fluidly between abstraction and impressionistic. Her paintings evolve thro
 ugh layered colour and an intuitive process\, reflecting a deeply personal
  exploration of place\, experience\, and transformation.
LOCATION:Ann Rosmarin Fine Art
URL:https://annrosmarin.com/fineart/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
