BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vallejo Pista Sa Nayon
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T180000
UID:2603257QTbMyrRh0ariq7ObFqGvQ
DESCRIPTION:Vallejo Pista Sa Nayon \\(“Town Festival”\\) is Vallejo’
 s largest annual Filipino cultural celebration\, honoring Philippine Indep
 endence Day through food\, music\, dance\, and cultural performances that 
 showcase the richness and diversity of the islands. 2026 marks our 40th an
 niversary of Vallejo Pista Sa Nayon.\n\nJoin thousands in celebrating heri
 tage\, community\, and unity—a vibrant gathering rooted in tradition and
  shared pride.\n\nJoin us for a one-of-a-kind festival!  Attendees will l
 earn about the islands and experience a deeper dive into their history\, t
 raditions\, history\, food\, language\, and more.  Our festival hopes to 
 inspire and strengthen families and the larger community.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_
 \n\nParking is limited. We highly encourage early arrival\, carpooling and
  taking the free SF Bay Ferry between downtown Vallejo and Mare Island.
LOCATION:Mare Island Waterfront Promenade
URL:https://www.vallejopistasanayon.com/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Creative Photography Workshop at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T150000
UID:260312823Erq1r-0aeNE0E2Kb_hA
DESCRIPTION:Discover and master the potential of your iPhone camera with p
 rofessional photographers Susan and Neil Silverman of silvermansphotogra
 phy.com.  \n\nThe first half of the workshop \\(held inside the House of 
 Happy Walls Museum\\) will cover settings\, filters\, exposure\, focus\, s
 hutter speeds\, panoramas\, macro\, close ups\, and portraits\, with an em
 phasis on the creative and artistic side of photography.  The morning ven
 ue is reached by a narrow staircase to the second floor. Call 707-938-5216
  with questions about access.\n\nThe group will then move outdoors to put 
 into practical use the things we have just talked about.  Bring your lunc
 h for a quick picnic.   \n\nParticipants will leave with some potential 
 great images\, confidence\, and expanded knowledge in using the iPhone cam
 era to capture images that are real “keepers.”\n\nAll levels of photog
 raphy experience are welcome\, as are both iPhones and Androids \\(iPhones
  will be used for demonstrations\\).
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/creative-photography-wo
 rkshop-at-jack-london-state-historic-park/18318972/2026-06-06T09
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
