BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2026 Solano County Fair
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T200000
UID:26033008lfukJTRUS04EXkVPBiEw
DESCRIPTION:77th Annual Solano County Fair\n\nJoin us June 11&ndash\;14\, 
 2026 at the Solano County Fairgrounds in Vallejo for the 77th Annual Solan
 o County Fair. This year's theme\, &ldquo\;Stars\, Stripes\, and Carnival 
 Lights\,&rdquo\; celebrates America's 250th anniversary with four days of 
 carnival rides\, live entertainment\, fair food\, agricultural exhibits\, 
 livestock shows\, and interactive experiences for all ages.\n\nIn addition
  to general fair admission\, don't miss the exciting Arena Concert Series 
 featuring nightly live performances\, including Thursday's Julia Neville c
 oncert\, Friday's concert as well as the high-energy Saturday Demolition D
 erby &mdash\; both held in the Fairgrounds arena.\n\nA long-standing commu
 nity tradition\, the Solano County Fair brings together families\, friends
 \, and neighbors for a festive summer experience that showcases the region
 's rich heritage and spirit.\n\nTicket Information\n\nTickets are valid fo
 r the specific event date selected \\(Arena Concert or Demolition Derby\\)
 .\n\nEvery person entering will need a ticket.  Zero dollar tickets availa
 ble for Children under 6 available. Ages verified at the gates. \n\nPresal
 e ends at Midnight on June 10\, 2026.\n\nNo re-entry after 10:00 p.m. \\(S
 unday: no entry or re-entry after 9:00 p.m.\\).\n\nMerchandise ordered onl
 ine may be picked up at the Fair merchandise booth during event hours.\n\n
 Fair Hours\n\nThursday: 4:00 p.m. &ndash\; 10:00 p.m.\n\nFriday: 12:00 p.m
 . &ndash\; 10:00 p.m.\n\nSaturday: 12:00 p.m. &ndash\; 10:00 p.m.\n\nSunda
 y: 12:00 p.m. &ndash\; 10:00 p.m. \\(No entry or re-entry after 9:00 p.m.\
 \)\n\nParking Information\n\nParking is not included and must be purchased
  separately.\n\nADA parking is limited and available on a first-come\, fir
 st-served basis.
LOCATION:Solano County Fairgrounds
URL:https://tickets.eventhub.net/e/2026-solano-county-fair?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Napa Valley Jazz Getaway
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T000000
UID:260327kef86rrG4ku05tx5xrwABA
DESCRIPTION:Jonathan is the product of the Western World. \n\n At thirteen
 \, Jonathan's talents caught the ears and eyes of British record producer 
 Clive Caulder. He was signed to Caulder's Jive Records and as the old clic
 he goes\, the rest is history. \n\n \n\n Jonathan's first single broke dow
 n racial barriers\, becoming the first song by a black artist to be played
  by white radio stations in South Africa. Because Jive was headquartered i
 n England\, Jonathan decided to move there to focus on his recording caree
 r. His commitment to his craft paid off with his self-titled debut album\,
  which received a Grammy nomination for the pop hit &quot\;Lies.&quot\; \n
 \n \n\n Jonathan's ability to blend his roots in African music with wester
 n pop sensibilities would be a trademark of many albums to follow\, though
  never more refined than in his latest release. \n\n \n\n For example\, th
 e first single from Jonathan is a rendition of the folk-rock classic &quot
 \;Fire and Rain.&quot\; Butler breathes new life into this classic\, infus
 ing the vocals with intensity\, as subtle as it is powerful. The musical a
 rrangement is lively and soulful\, indicative of his roots in World music.
  &quot\;Fire and Rain&quot\; is already garnering accolades from top radio
  programmers. Lori Lewis\, program director for WSMJ in Baltimore states\,
  &quot\;It literally gave me a lump in my throat. I walked into the studio
  and introduced it live on air. Vocals this great are really rare.&quot\;
LOCATION:Blue Note Summer Sessions at Meritage Resort
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107690478?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
