BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rise With Pride – Featuring J. Graves\, Kochina Rude & Tila Pia
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T220000
UID:260515zV9OeP7ILEa8W9QeoJGfJQ
DESCRIPTION:Great — here’s the full updated listing with that version 
 worked in:\n\nWe Rise With Pride Concert & Drag Show\n\nSonoma Valley Prid
 e presents **We Rise With Pride**\, the first annual Pride Concert and Dra
 g Show at the historic Sebastiani Theatre in Sonoma.\n\nKicking off Sonoma
  Valley Pride weekend\, this high-energy evening brings together queer mus
 ic\, drag\, performance\, and community for a night of unapologetic expres
 sion and Pride. Sonoma Valley Pride is an annual celebration in the heart 
 of Sonoma Valley focused on building queer spaces\, uplifting LGBTQIA+ vis
 ibility\, and creating joyful community-centered events in a region where 
 queer entertainment and gathering spaces are still growing.\n\nHeadlining 
 the night is **J. Graves**\, a queer\, non-binary-led band out of Portland
  known for their guitar-driven sound\, bold vocals\, and high-energy live 
 performances. Blending dance-punk\, post-punk\, and garage rock influences
 \, J. Graves brings a sound that will appeal to fans of **Yeah Yeah Yeahs*
 * and **The Kills** — rhythmic\, electric\, and built for the stage.\n\n
 The evening also features fierce drag from two Bay Area legends: **Kochina
  Rude**\, Sonoma County native\, host\, and performer\, and **Tila Pia**\,
  an infamous stunt queen who has turned looks from Hawaii to New York.\n\n
 Expect a show that moves between live music\, drag\, and moments that brin
 g the whole room in. This is not something Sonoma sees every day.\n\nThe c
 oncert is also a fundraiser for Sonoma Valley Pride\, supporting future ev
 ents\, visibility\, community programming\, and the continued growth of Pr
 ide in Sonoma Valley. Every ticket helps build what comes next.\n\nCome re
 ady to dance\, show up\, and be part of it.\n\n**Tickets:** General admiss
 ion tickets are $35. Special $15 youth tickets are available for attendees
  under 21 as part of Sonoma Valley Pride’s commitment to keeping Pride a
 ccessible. Alcohol will be available for purchase for guests 21+\, with sp
 ecial non-alcoholic offerings available for youth and under-21 attendees.\
 n\n**Performers:** J. Graves — Headliner Kochina Rude — Host and Perfo
 rmer Tila Pia — Performer / Stunt Queen
LOCATION:Sebastiani Theatre
URL:https://www.sonomavalleypride.com/events/first-annual-pride-concert-fe
 aturing-j-graves-kochina-rude-tila-pia/?utm_source=bohemian&utm_medium=soc
 ial&utm_campaign=friday---rise-with-pride-live-concert-and-drag-show-featu
 ring-jgraves--drag--sebastiani-theatre&utm_content=friday-concert---bohemi
 an-event-listing
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Valley Pride
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T220000
UID:260515orkXsogmdUef6LSMlED1HQ
DESCRIPTION:Sonoma Valley Pride returns for a full weekend of queer joy\, 
 live entertainment\, community\, and Pride in the heart of Sonoma Valley.\
 n\nThis year’s celebration expands into a three-day Pride weekend\, brin
 ging together music\, drag\, dancing\, local artists\, food\, wine\, commu
 nity organizations\, and LGBTQIA+ visibility across Sonoma. Sonoma Valley 
 Pride is focused on building queer spaces\, creating joyful gathering plac
 es\, and bringing more LGBTQIA+ entertainment and community-centered progr
 amming to the region.\n\nThe weekend kicks off Friday\, June 12\, with **W
 e Rise With Pride**\, Sonoma Valley Pride’s first annual Concert and Dra
 g Show at the historic Sebastiani Theatre. The evening features headliner 
 **J. Graves**\, a queer\, non-binary-led band from Portland known for thei
 r guitar-driven sound\, bold vocals\, and high-energy live performances. B
 lending dance-punk\, post-punk\, and garage rock influences\, J. Graves br
 ings a sound that will appeal to fans of **Yeah Yeah Yeahs** and **The Kil
 ls** — rhythmic\, electric\, and built for the stage. The night also fea
 tures drag from Bay Area legends **Kochina Rude**\, Sonoma County native\,
  host\, and performer\, and **Tila Pia**\, an infamous stunt queen who has
  turned looks from Hawaii to New York.\n\nOn Saturday\, June 13\, the cele
 bration continues with a Pride Dance Party at **The General’s Daughter**
 \, inviting the community to keep the weekend moving with music\, dancing\
 , and celebration.\n\nOn Sunday\, June 14\, Sonoma Valley Pride gathers on
  the historic Sonoma Plaza for a free community Pride Festival featuring l
 ive performances\, speakers\, queer art\, local vendors\, food\, wine\, an
 d community connection. With a bigger stage\, more room to gather\, and ev
 en more ways to celebrate\, the Plaza Festival is designed for friends\, f
 amilies\, chosen families\, locals\, visitors\, and allies to come togethe
 r in the spirit of Pride.\n\nFrom the theatre to the dance floor to the Pl
 aza lawn\, Sonoma Valley Pride weekend is a celebration of queer artistry\
 , visibility\, belonging\, and joy in Sonoma Valley. Come ready to dance\,
  show up\, and be part of what comes next.
LOCATION:Sonoma Plaza
URL:https://www.sonomavalleypride.com/?utm_source=bohemian&utm_medium=soci
 al&utm_campaign=pride-weekend---2026-svp-pride-festival-&utm_content=svp--
 -bohemian
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rise With Pride featuring J. Graves\, Kochina Rude & Tila Pia
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T220000
UID:260515b7VidGMKzE6-lB-iASFduA
DESCRIPTION:We Rise With Pride Concert & Drag Show\n\nSonoma Valley Pride 
 presents **We Rise With Pride**\, the first annual Pride Concert and Drag 
 Show at the historic Sebastiani Theatre in Sonoma.\n\nKicking off Sonoma V
 alley Pride weekend\, this high-energy evening brings together queer music
 \, drag\, performance\, and community for a night of unapologetic expressi
 on and Pride. Sonoma Valley Pride is an annual celebration in the heart of
  Sonoma Valley focused on building queer spaces\, uplifting LGBTQIA+ visib
 ility\, and creating joyful community-centered events in a region where qu
 eer entertainment and gathering spaces are still growing.\n\nHeadlining th
 e night is **J. Graves**\, a queer\, non-binary-led band out of Portland k
 nown for their guitar-driven sound\, bold vocals\, and high-energy live pe
 rformances. Blending dance-punk\, post-punk\, and garage rock influences\,
  J. Graves brings a sound that will appeal to fans of **Yeah Yeah Yeahs** 
 and **The Kills** — rhythmic\, electric\, and built for the stage.\n\nTh
 e evening also features fierce drag from two Bay Area legends: **Kochina R
 ude**\, Sonoma County native\, host\, and performer\, and **Tila Pia**\, a
 n infamous stunt queen who has turned looks from Hawaii to New York.\n\nEx
 pect a show that moves between live music\, drag\, and moments that bring 
 the whole room in. This is not something Sonoma sees every day.\n\nThe con
 cert is also a fundraiser for Sonoma Valley Pride\, supporting future even
 ts\, visibility\, community programming\, and the continued growth of Prid
 e in Sonoma Valley. Every ticket helps build what comes next.\n\nCome read
 y to dance\, show up\, and be part of it.\n\n**Tickets:** General admissio
 n tickets are $35. Special $15 youth tickets are available for attendees u
 nder 21 as part of Sonoma Valley Pride’s commitment to keeping Pride acc
 essible. Alcohol will be available for purchase for guests 21+\, with spec
 ial non-alcoholic offerings available for youth and under-21 attendees.\n\
 n**Performers:** J. Graves — Headliner Kochina Rude — Host and Perform
 er Tila Pia — Performer / Stunt Queen
LOCATION:Sebastiani Theatre
URL:https://www.sonomavalleypride.com/events/first-annual-pride-concert-fe
 aturing-j-graves-kochina-rude-tila-pia/?utm_source=press-democrat&utm_medi
 um=social&utm_campaign=friday---rise-with-pride-live-concert-and-drag-show
 -featuring-jgraves--drag--sebastiani-theatre&utm_content=friday---press-de
 mocrat
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wine Tails Trail at Cuvaison Winery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T170000
UID:260508HFHGw3qZ6k-Cqs2pdwHByw
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a new way to experience Cuvaison with your canine compan
 ion on the Wine Tails Trail. This self-guided vineyard walk winds just und
 er a mile through our Los Carneros estate\, with QR code stops highlightin
 g the history of our vines and winemaking. Guests begin their adventure by
  checking in with our Concierge for a map and orientation before setting o
 ff on the trail.\n\nAfter the walk\, return to the estate and enjoy a seat
 ed tasting of our current release wines\, while your pup relaxes by your s
 ide and enjoys a selection of “Barkuterie.” The Wine Tails Trail is a 
 chance to stretch your legs\, explore the vineyard\, and savor Cuvaison in
  the company of your best friend.\n\nWhen booking this experience\, please
  plan for the dog walk to begin at the time you select. The walk itself av
 erages about 45 minutes\, though you’ll also check in with our Concierge
  before and after\, as well as complete a quick waiver at the start. Your 
 wine tasting will be scheduled 60 minutes after your selected walk time\, 
 allowing a smooth transition from the trail back to your seated experience
 .\n\nGroup Size: Up to 4 guests\, including non-tasters\n\nDuration: Pleas
 e allow 120 minutes for this experience
LOCATION:Cuvaison Experience Salon\, Outdoors Only
URL:https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings 
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
