BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nancy Fawson Music
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T000000
UID:260307Mgju6rLxuUWdAH0lDmgKCQ
DESCRIPTION:Nancy Fawson is a powerhouse Bay Area-based vocalist and songw
 riter whose musical roots run deep in soul\, R&B and rock. Raised on the i
 conic sounds of Sam Cooke\, Etta James\, Aretha Franklin\, Chaka Khan\, St
 evie Wonder\, and Amy Winehouse\, Nancy’s musical influences have left a
 n indelible imprint on her voice and style. With a unique\, soulful tone a
 nd a passion for heartfelt expression\, Nancy connects with her audience o
 n a profound level—delivering each song with purity\, emotion\, and auth
 enticity.\n\nNancy’s vocal range spans across a variety of genres\, incl
 uding soul\, funk\, blues\, R&B\, and rock\, allowing her to bring versati
 lity to every performance. Whether performing with a duo or full band\, sh
 e engages audiences with her compelling stage presence and soulful deliver
 y.\n\nAs the lead singer of the popular Marin-based blues\, soul\, and fun
 k band Corner Pocket\, Nancy continues to captivate crowds with her raw en
 ergy and dedication to the craft. In addition to live performances\, she i
 s also available for recording session work\, offering her talents as both
  a lead and background vocalist.\n\nWith a sound that blends classic influ
 ences with modern flair\, Nancy Fawson is an artist whose voice you won’
 t soon forget.
LOCATION:Rio Nido Roadhouse
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107881729?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Country Summer Music Festival 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T000000
UID:260224hmrjQ_byOEWOJqEKwqN_4w
DESCRIPTION:Country music superstar Cole Swindell\, who Rolling Stone has 
 called “a proven hit-maker\,” has solidified himself as a hit songwrit
 er\, recording artist and headlining performer over the past eleven years.
  With his latest single “Forever To Me” from his upcoming fifth studio
  album\, Spanish Moss\, just hitting No. 1\, the multi-Platinum award winn
 er has now racked up 13 No. 1 singles as an artist – 14 as a songwriter.
  Twelve of Swindell’s 13 No. 1 singles have been certified Platinum by t
 he RIAA with three being 3X Platinum \\(“Chillin’ It\,” “You Shoul
 d Be Here\,” and “She Had Me At Heads Carolina”\\) and two being 2X 
 Platinum \\(“Ain’t Worth The Whiskey” and “Break Up In The End”\
 \).\n\nSwindell\, who The Tennessean called a “hard charging competitor 
 armed with a mastery of the art of the craft\, tirelessly looking for ways
  to improve his work” charted three back-to-back\, Platinum-certified\, 
 multi-week No. 1 hits off his fourth studio album\, Stereotype: “Single 
 Saturday Night\,” “Never Say Never” \\(with Lainey Wilson\\) and the
  five-week 3x Platinum chart-topper “She Had Me At Heads Carolina” tha
 t garnered three ACM Awards for Single of the Year and Song of the Year \\
 (as songwriter and artist\\)\, an iHeart Music Award for Country Song of t
 he Year and received a nomination for Musical Event of the Year for “She
  Had Me At Heads Carolina” with Jo Dee Messina for the 57th CMA Awards. 
 He released a special duet remix of his smash “She Had Me At Heads Carol
 ina” featuring Messina that produced multiple award nominations and is i
 ncluded on his deluxe album Stereotype Broken\, which also includes his 20
 23 Top 10 single “Drinkaby.”
LOCATION:ARENA CRIS BECK
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107983518?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sister Act
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T220000
UID:250804dvqT8X0RlEm9yBscc_QjRQ
DESCRIPTION:**A Disco Diva\, a Choir in Crisis\, and a Whole Lot of Soul!*
 *\n\n***“One of the season’s happiest surprises.”* —Elisabeth Vinc
 entelli for New York Post**\n\n***Sister Act* is the high-energy musical c
 omedy based on the beloved 1992 film. Featuring an electrifying Alan Menke
 n score infused with disco and gospel beats\, this feel-good show is a cel
 ebration of music\, sisterhood\, and second chances.**\n\n**When disco div
 a Deloris Van Cartier witnesses a crime\, she’s forced into hiding—in 
 a convent! Disguised as a nun\, she transforms the struggling choir with h
 er powerhouse voice\, helping them find their sound while discovering her 
 own. Nominated for five Tony Awards\, *Sister Act* is a joyful\, soul-stir
 ring spectacle that proves music—and a little mischief—can work miracl
 es!**\n\nThursdays\, Fridays & Saturdays @ 7:30pm\, Saturdays and Sundays 
 at 2:00pm Run Time: Two hours\, 30 mins including intermission\n\nThursday
 s Adult $33Fri/Sat Eve Adult $44.95\; Senior $38.95\; Under 18 $31.95Sat/S
 un Matinee Adult $55.95\; Senior $48.95Value seating $37.95\\*All prices i
 nclude fees\n\n(707) 523-4185\n\n**boxoffice@6thstreetplayhouse.com**
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/2025-26/sister-act/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
