BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Free Speech Benefit for Sonoma County Radio (Tom Lehrer music revu
 e)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T213000
UID:260530YyBoxAShhkaqTsFdQowOcw
DESCRIPTION:If you value public media\, free expression\, and witty\, irre
 verent music—get your tickets for the ***Totally Incorrect Players*** pe
 rformance at Sebastiani Theater—a rousing musical evening celebrating th
 e work of legendary satirist **Tom Lehrer**. Their 90-minute musical revue
  has sold out every venue and breathes new—and very silly—life into To
 m’s legacy of brilliant songs.  All proceeds will be donated to local r
 adio stations KSVY 91.3 FM and KRCB 104.9 FM NorCal Public Media in suppor
 t of local public broadcasting in Sonoma County.\n\nFor over a decade\, To
 m Lehrer was an international sensation. He produced six studio and live a
 lbums\, and is regarded as one of the most respected and admired satirists
  of our time.  He has been cited as a major influence by Stephen Colbert\
 , John Oliver\, Randy Newman\, Monty Python\, Mark Russel\, Weird Al Yanko
 vic\, Bo Burnham\, Donald Fagen and Walter Becker and countless other writ
 ers\, performers and artists.\n\nAt a time when free speech is being threa
 tened throughout our country—and the world—the messages of Lehrer’s 
 songs are more timely than ever.  His ability to highlight the absurdity 
 of modern life\, and the wild characters that inhabit it\, through the pow
 er of his shrewd satire inspires us all to empower ourselves at a time whe
 n we need it the most.  A need made even more poignant by the untimely de
 parture of Stephen Colbert.  And just like Colbert\, this show is as rele
 ntlessly fun and funny as it is remarkably relevant.
LOCATION:Sebastiani Theatre
URL:https://events.sebastianitheatre.com/an-evening-of-the-twisted-songs-o
 f-tom-lehrer/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
