BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Art of Game Design
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260617T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260617T160000
UID:260604xqy_dt_-pkeyelllViGHnw
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 13\\+\n\nGames are one of today's most dynamic creative mediums\,
  blending storytelling\, systems thinking\, and player experience. In this
  hands-on workshop\, participants will step into the role of a game design
 er&mdash\;learning how rules\, mechanics\, and narrative work together to 
 shape meaningful play. Through guided exercises\, you'll explore player-ce
 ntered design\, discover how rules themselves can become a form of artisti
 c expression\, and experiment with rapid prototyping techniques. By the en
 d of the session\, you'll have designed and play-tested your own original 
 tabletop game using simple materials\, gaining practical tools for turning
  ideas into engaging interactive experiences.\n\nThis workshop is located 
 in the classroom. \n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nPryce Jones is an artist\, de
 signer\, and educator whose work explores how people experience stories ac
 ross digital\, physical\, and interactive environments. With a background 
 in architecture\, video games\, and immersive media\, he began his career 
 at Gensler before spending nearly two decades as an environment artist and
  art director with studios including LucasArts\, Eidos\, Activision\, and 
 Gazillion Entertainment. His current practice bridges fine art\, creative 
 placemaking\, and emerging technologies to engage communities around histo
 ry and identity. He has served as founding MFA Director at the Academy of 
 Art University and now teaches Game Arts at the California College of the 
 Arts\, mentoring the next generation of artists and designers.\n\nLearn Mo
 re: \n\nwww.prycejonesart.com
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-art-gamedesign
 ?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Foundations of Oil Painting: Materials & Methods
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260617T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260617T210000
UID:260604t2Rcr60-tUiKz170Wni4vQ
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 13\\+\n\nCurious about oil painting but not sure where to start? 
 This beginner-friendly workshop demystifies the essentials\, introducing y
 ou to the materials\, tools\, and core techniques that make oil painting s
 o rich and versatile. You'll learn how to set up your palette\, understand
  mediums and surfaces\, and explore foundational methods like layering\, b
 lending\, and brushwork. With guided instruction and hands-on exploration\
 , you'll gain the confidence to begin your own oil painting practice and d
 iscover the unique beauty of working with this timeless medium.\n\nThis wo
 rkshop is located in the classroom. \n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nMaggie Parr
  began her career at Walt Disney Imagineering\, working as a show designer
  on attractions for Toontown and Animal Kingdom. After leaving Disney to f
 ocus on painting\, she continued as an independent contractor while expand
 ing into book illustration\, murals\, portraits\, comics\, and television 
 writing. She trained in classical painting with artists including Steve Hu
 ston\, Cheryl Kline\, Steven Assael\, Jeremy Lipking\, and Joseph Q. Daily
 \, later earning an MFA. She now teaches students of all levels while main
 taining an active painting practice.\n\nLearn More: \n\nwww.maggieparr.com
 www.parrcreate.com@maggieparrart
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-oil-painting-f
 oundations?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Get Hooked! A Mother-Daughter Rug Hooking Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260617T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260617T120000
UID:260604kjMm4oV9kEeK-rAPuO9Inw
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 10\\+\n\nJoin Emma Logan and her mother Laura Pierce for a warm\,
  welcoming introduction to the timeless craft of traditional rug hooking. 
 In this hands-on workshop\, participants will create their own &ldquo\;mug
  rug&rdquo\;&mdash\;a small\, decorative coaster&mdash\;using scrap fabric
  and embroidery hoops\, while learning foundational techniques passed down
  through generations. Designed to demystify a craft that can feel intimida
 ting or expensive\, this experience reveals how accessible\, creative\, an
 d deeply satisfying rug hooking can be. Along the way\, you'll connect wit
 h heritage skills\, explore texture and color\, and leave with a beautiful
  handmade piece. No prior experience needed.\n\nThis class is located in t
 he classroom. \n\nTeacher provides: \n\nLinen\, hoops\, hooks\, wool\n\nAb
 out the Teachers: \n\nBased in Petaluma\, Laura Pierce and Emma Logan are 
 a mother/daughter team with over 30 years of teaching experience between t
 hem. While Laura focuses on rug hooking and other fiber work\, Emma's art 
 practice includes using clay\, paper\, and fiber materials to make sculptu
 re and installation work. Both prioritize individual learning in their tea
 ching styles and have worked collaboratively to run rug camps and one-day 
 classes. Coming from a long line of makers\, they are passionate about han
 dicrafts and helping others learn new skills through projects designed to 
 be accessible and inspirational for any level.\n\nLearn More: \n\nwww.emma
 roselogan.comlaurawp.wordpress.comwww.flyingdoghookery.com
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-get-hooked?aff
 =cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Expanding Watercolor: Innovative Materials & Techniques
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260617T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260617T200000
UID:2606040MNGZDhjy0a4gyb8yKg4wA
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 18 and over\n\nAbout this Class:\n\nAn informative presentation b
 y Kei Weaver that reimagines watercolor as a bold\, experimental medium fo
 r personal expression. Moving beyond traditional rules\, Weaver shares inn
 ovative approaches to combining watercolor with ink\, mica\, and mixed med
 ia while exploring unconventional tools like watercolor sticks\, dot cards
 \, and alternative surfaces such as Aquabord and aluminum panels. Through 
 demonstrations and insights into texture\, granulation\, color mixing\, an
 d material compatibility\, this talk empowers artists to break free from c
 onvention and discover new creative possibilities within watercolor.\n\nTh
 is lecture is located in the Main Gallery.\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nKei W
 eaver \\(they/them\\) is a nonbinary visual artist based in Petaluma. Thei
 r paintings of poppies\, Sonoma County landscapes\, and anime-inspired cha
 racters combine expressive\, heavily pigmented watercolor with the decisiv
 eness of black ink. Kei has previously taught college-level courses while 
 studying at Carnegie Mellon University\, Cornell University\, and the Univ
 ersity of Maryland - College Park.\n\nLearn more about Kei:\n\nwww.thestud
 iokei.com@thestudiokei
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pacacademy-expanding-water
 color?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
