BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Santa Rosa Wednesday Night Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260617T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260617T000000
UID:260526NxWMjXtD1E6GEjd_6lukww
DESCRIPTION:The Santa Rosa Wednesday Night Market is a beloved free commun
 ity event that's been a tradition for 37 years and brings people together 
 to celebrate local culture\, small businesses\, and the vibrant spirit of 
 downtown. Our mission is to create an inclusive\, welcoming public space w
 here residents and visitors can gather to enjoy great food\, live entertai
 nment\, and unique local vendors while supporting the economic and social 
 health of our city. This lively open-air street fair features a curated se
 lection of local artisans\, farmers\, food vendors\, and community organiz
 ations. Guests can enjoy live music and performances\, explore handmade go
 ods\, discover fresh local products\, and connect with the people who make
  Sonoma County special. Families are especially welcome. The Market includ
 es a dedicated Kids Zone with free activities for children\, interactive e
 xperiences\, and opportunities for learning and play. Local nonprofit orga
 nizations also participate each week\, sharing information about their pro
 grams and helping strengthen connections across the community. The Wednesd
 ay Night Market is more than an event-it's a celebration of community\, cr
 eativity\, and the local businesses and organizations that help Santa Rosa
  thrive.
LOCATION:Old Courthouse Square
URL:https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/#jlupcoming-events
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Acoustic Sunsets
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260617T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260617T000000
UID:260526mWHQ8hSKQEO2EEcvN7ghfA
DESCRIPTION:Acoustic Sunsets returns for its third season! From May 6 thro
 ugh September 16\\*\, the Garden extends its hours Wednesday evenings unti
 l 8:00 pm. Each evening features live music by Bay Area musicians in our o
 utdoor amphitheater from 5:30-7:30 pm. Guests are invited to bring picnics
  and well-behaved dogs on leash\, enjoy wine tastings with local vintners\
 , and unwind in the Garden's beautiful\, natural setting. New this year! M
 onthly Noche Latina nights celebrating Latin music and culture in conjunct
 ion with the special exhibition Spirit Guides: Fantastical Creatures from 
 the Workshop of Jacobo and María Ángeles. Free for Sonoma Botanical Gard
 en members and included in general admission for non-members. This is a dr
 op-in program and tickets are sold at check-in\, no advance registration i
 s required. \\*No concerts June 10 or July 1
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/#jlupcoming-events
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Santa Rosa Original Certified Farmers Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260617T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260617T000000
UID:260504TLjKwBRYK0ihwS-hr67S6Q
DESCRIPTION:The Santa Rosa Original Certified Farmers Market is a year-rou
 nd Saturday tradition in Sonoma County\, bringing together local farmers\,
  ranchers\, food artisans\, and neighbors from 8:30 a.m. to 1 p.m. This is
  not just a place to shop\, it's a place to connect directly with the peop
 le who grow your food. As a Slow Food Sonoma County award recipient\, the 
 market prioritizes integrity\, seasonality\, and true farm-to-community re
 lationships. Expect peak-season produce harvested just hours before market
 \, pasture-raised meats\, fresh flowers\, artisan breads\, handcrafted goo
 ds\, and thoughtfully prepared foods that reflect the region's agricultura
 l richness. Visitors can stroll the vibrant open-air market\, sample local
  flavors\, and experience Sonoma County's food culture in its most authent
 ic form. Families\, chefs\, and weekend explorers alike gather here to dis
 cover what's growing now and to support small farms that keep our local fo
 od system strong. Open every Saturday\, rain or shine\, the Santa Rosa Ori
 ginal Certified Farmers Market is a cornerstone of the community and a mus
 t-visit stop for anyone wanting to taste\, shop\, and experience Sonoma Co
 unty at its freshest.
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/#jlupcoming-events
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
