SUMMARY:Back pOrchEstra!- at Murphy's Sonoma June 18\, Thu 7:00-9:00
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T210000
UID:2605110ZwAu_UZEEaYem9BXuuCIg
DESCRIPTION:American Roots party with Back pOrchEstra!- at Murphy's Sonoma
  June 18\, Thu 7:00-9:00\n\nJoin us for... some Indie and roots rock and t
 he American Roots that inspired it... with Candy Girard\, Tim Eschliman\, 
 Gary Potterton\, Jen Rund and Luis Rodriguez in a mostly-acoustic format o
 n resonator guitar\, violin\, bass\, drums\, percussion\, dobro & Telecast
 er\n\nCelebrating the new "Stories In The Heart" album\, listen now!: http
 s://orcd.co/5xga7nr\n\nSingle out now too\, "Ever Think About It:" https:/
 /orcd.co/qo5579q\n\nLPs\, CDs\, and USB-Music Cards available all over\, i
 ncluding https://www.globerecords.com\n\nVince's Hot Picks \\(Best of 2026
 \\): "... a warm\, road-worn album that leans into rich acoustic tones whi
 le freely bending genres without ever breaking the feel. Built around a mo
 stly unplugged framework\, the record draws from country blues\, roots roc
 k\, Zydeco\, Tex-Mex\, New Orleans rhythms\, Motown soul\, singer-songwrit
 er traditions\, and even Brazilian textures\, all woven together with an e
 asy confidence that sounds earned\, not assembled."\n\n464 1st St E\, Sono
 ma\, CA 95476 \\(707\\) 935-0660 ...with plenty of outdoor seating that in
 cludes both Murphy's Irish Pub and Taste of the Himalayas.\n\n...songs fro
 m all over the map... originals and reworked classics by Hank Williams\, T
 aj Mahal\, Dan Hicks\, Big Bill Broonzy\, Bob Wills\, Jimmy Reed\, Joseph 
 & Cleome Falcon and Bobby Charles.\n\nwhat a sample? check out the "Dusty 
 Road I'm On" video: https://youtu.be/jj0IIkUyrE4 ...a twangy roots rock nu
 mber with a Cajun flavor and hints of Jesse Ed Davis and Sid Page....\n\n"
 ...everything from alt. rock to cajun\, to country\, to Brownie Ford era W
 estern Swing. But the thing that keeps this set together is their excellen
 t songwriting full of smooth never-miss-a-beat lines and vivid imagery. It
 's a studio album but it sure does have a back porch jam band feel to it" 
 - Calvin Powers\, WHUP-FM\, americanamusicshow.com\,\n\nmore at... https:/
 /www.BackpOrchEstra.com\n\nBandCamp: https://backporchestra.bandcamp.com\n
 \nyouTube: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLOTwG2XEiO2O8c0dEI-7hlpI
 8nr7apiNf\n\nBluesky: https://bsky.app/profile/backporchestra.bsky.social\
 n\nReverb Nation: https://www.reverbnation.com/backporchestra\n\nFacebook:
  https://www.facebook.com/BackPorchEstra/\n\nInstagram: https://www.instag
 ram.com/backporchestra/\n\n\\#rootsrock\n\n\\#americanrootsmusic\n\n\\#ame
 ricanamusic\n\n\\#rockabillymusic\n\n\\#twangyguitar\n\n\\#backporchestra\
 n\n\\#acousticmusic\n\n\\#adultalbumalternative\n\n\\#singersongwriter\n\n
 \\#folkmusic\n\n\\#folkrock
