BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Zines for Teens
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T160000
UID:260604YWNI1k9cdkyYttFugT8I2Q
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 13-19\n\nJump into a high-energy\, hands-on zine-making experienc
 e where teens bring their ideas to life through bold visuals and DIY story
 telling. Using hand-drawing\, collage\, found papers\, and simple binding 
 techniques\, participants create their own self-published mini magazines f
 rom start to finish. Whether the message is political\, personal\, social\
 , or playful\, this workshop empowers creative voices to be seen and share
 d&mdash\;resulting in a one-of-a-kind zine that's as expressive and unique
  as its maker.\n\nThis class is located in the classroom. \n\nAbout the Te
 acher: \n\nAnn Ledo-Lane is an interdisciplinary artist\, educator and joy
 crafter. Born in the Bay Area\, and currently living in a little redwood f
 orest in Marin\, she focuses on cultivating joy through daily creative pra
 ctices that intersect nature\, memory\, and the everyday. A long-time crea
 tive educator in arts-centered public schools\, Ann is delighted to engage
  in artistic play through pop up arts workshops\, community arts spaces\, 
 and on the college level\, ensuring creative practices are accessible to m
 any and a tool for equity\, personal wellness\, and connection. Ann lives 
 with her two children\, dog\, and husband\, sculptor\, Sebastian Lane\, wh
 o all share her love of outdoor adventuring\, making\, and chair design.
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pacacademy-zines-for-teens
 ?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
