BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Blind Expression: Discovering Your Inner Abstract Voice
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260619T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260619T160000
UID:260604t5esm1hvXk67DFyOZprWNw
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 10 and up\n\nAbout this Class:\n\nAn acrylic painting workshop fo
 r teens and adults of all skill levels that guides participants through an
  intuitive\, judgment-free creative process. Beginning with intention sett
 ing and eyes-closed painting\, students generate spontaneous marks that th
 ey later develop into abstract compositions with conscious refinement\, al
 l while working within simple constraints like a limited color palette. Th
 e experience emphasizes tapping into subconscious imagery\, building confi
 dence in one's unique artistic voice\, and exploring meaning beyond litera
 l representation. The workshop concludes with a reflective group activity 
 where participants anonymously share written interpretations of their work
  and collectively match them to the paintings\, fostering empathy\, connec
 tion\, and deeper appreciation for diverse perspectives in art.\n\nThis cl
 ass is located in the Main Gallery.\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nAmanda Squia
 ssi Coffin is a Brazilian-born artist based in Northern California\, with 
 a background in Architecture and Urbanism and experience as a staging desi
 gner for leading firms in the San Francisco Bay Area. Her journey into pai
 nting began in 2023 during maternity leave\, when a quiet moment of curios
 ity turned into a deep passion and ultimately a new career path. Known for
  her bold\, expressive abstract style rooted in intuition and movement\, A
 manda creates work that evolves organically&mdash\;allowing shapes\, color
 s\, and patterns to guide each piece rather than following a predetermined
  plan. Her artwork invites a sense of freedom\, self-discovery\, and play\
 , encouraging others to trust their instincts and embrace the unknown. Thr
 ough her teaching\, she aims to create a supportive space where students c
 an explore their own creative voice\, let go of perfection\, and experienc
 e the joy of painting without limits.\n\nLearn more about Amanda:\n\nwww.f
 ofutaart.com@fofutaart
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pacacademy-inner-abstract-
 voice?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
