UID:260528lKCZegHeXUWpE2-SbK6LDA
DESCRIPTION:Ready to bring the energy\, rhythm\, and joy of Brazil into yo
 ur life? Join us for an exciting Samba Beginner Workshop designed specific
 ally for absolute beginners. No dance experience or partner required!\n\nL
 ed by the incredible duo Eric and Abigail\, you’ll dive into the vibran
 t world of Samba\, learning the foundational steps that will get you movin
 g with confidence.\n\nWhat You’ll Learn:\n\n• The Samba Basics: Maste
 r the core footwork and infectious rhythms.\n\n• Body Mechanics: Learn 
 how to find your bounce\, coordination\, and posture.\n\n• Musicality: 
 Understand the beat so you can dance naturally to any Samba track.\n\nWork
 shop Details:\n\n• Dates: Saturday\, June 20 & Saturday\, July 11\n\n
 • Time: 3:00 PM – 4:30 PM\n\n• Instructors: Eric & Abigail\n\n• L
 evel: Absolute Beginner \\(all fitness levels welcome!\\)\n\nSecure your 
 spot today and get ready to feel the rhythm.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/samba-beginner-workshop/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Paella at the Farm at Gold Ridge Organic Farms
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T150000
UID:260528VOQoS9iuN0K6K7UtWkvblg
DESCRIPTION:Savor the tastes of Spain with authentic paella by nationally 
 acclaimed\, locally owned Gerard's Paella\, made with locally sourced ingr
 edients and finished with our very own Gold Ridge Organic Farms Extra Virg
 in Olive Oil — all to the sounds of live Spanish guitar by Bay Area musi
 cian\, Jean-Paul.\n\nThere's plenty more to enjoy while you're here. Sampl
 e our award-winning organic olive oils and apple products\, cool off with
  an apple cider slushie or Straus ice cream drizzled with apple cider syru
 p\, and pick up something special from the Farm Shop. You can also meet th
 e makers behind Bella Rosa Coffee and Tienda Salsita\, two Sonoma County f
 avorites. \n\nTake a ride through our olive and apple orchards on the app
 le-themed decorative trolley. Tours depart at 11:30AM\, 12PM\, 12:30PM\, 1
 PM\, 1:30PM\, and 2PM.\n\nFree entry. Food\, drinks and orchard tour ticke
 ts available for purchase on the day. Paella available from 11:30AM to 2:3
 0PM or until sold out.
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://goldridgeorganicfarms.com/blogs/events/paella-at-the-farm
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
