BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Midsummer's Journey
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T160000
UID:260519ZKyol9L7aE6aYVFSkDcQsg
DESCRIPTION:WHAT: A Midsummer’s Journey – Oddities Market\n\n WHEN: 
  Saturday\, June 20th. 2026 10 am – 4 pm\n\n WHERE: Soap Cauldron/ Thr
 ee Sisters Apothecary and garden\n\n11830 Main St.\, Penngrove\, CA 94951\
 n\n Free event\n\n Special info: Vendor participation and performers will
  be provided in collaboration with the Menagerie & Oddities Expo.\n\n Tak
 e A Midsummer’s Journey in Penngrove -  June 20 \n\n Join A Midsummer
 ’s Journey and ODDventure to celebrate the Summer Solstice at Soap Cauld
 ron on June 20 from 10 am to 4 pm at Three Sisters Apothecary and garden i
 n Penngrove. \n\n Step into an immersive midsummer bazaar of wonder that
  blends artisan craftsmanship\, whimsical performance\, interactive ritual
 \, and community discovery. \n\n Guests are invited to wander\, explore\
 , and delight in curious\, magical\, and adventurous encounters along the 
 way. Designed as a welcoming\, come-and-go gathering\, Guests may particip
 ate as deeply or lightly as they wish.\n\n Throughout the day\, you will 
 encounter \\(sample of activities\\): \n\nOpening Journey Invocation\n\nI
 nsect Pinning Workshop\n\nDragon-Tail Performance\n\nAltar of Roads \\(hon
 oring origins\, crossroads\, & new journeys\\)\n\nWhimsical Roaming Creatu
 res\n\nOracles of the Crossroads\n\nA Wayfarer’s Gift Raffle\n\nTraveler
  Portrait Experience\n\nFirst-Arrival Journey Totes\n\nComplimentary Midsu
 mmer Provisions\n\nSilk\, a whimsical roaming character\n\nFeatured Musica
 l Performance by Aursjoen: AURSJOEN\n\n More details:\n\nInsect Pinning 
 Workshop — Insect pinning classes teach the art of preserving and displ
 aying insects\, such as butterflies and beetles\, using specialized entomo
 logy pins\, spreading boards\, and paper strips. Workshops often provide s
 pecimens\, kits\, and guidance on hydrating and positioning wings.\n\nFeat
 ured musical performance with AURSJOEN\, an ethereal artist musician based
  in San Francisco. https://aursjoen.bandcamp.com/album/strand\n\n Vendor 
 participation and performers will be provided in collaboration with the Me
 nagerie & Oddities Expo.\n\n For more information\, visit https://www.vis
 itpenngrove.com/a-midsummers-journey or call \\(707\\) 888-5659
LOCATION:Soap Caudron/Three Sisters Apothecary
URL:https://www.visitpenngrove.com/a-midsummers-journey 
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Live Music Saturday
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T200000
UID:260519YGU4RZ6vE0Gzb7lPzBLCQA
DESCRIPTION:Joyce Grant Vallejo local singer\, Joyce Grant returns to the 
 Ferry Taproom with her powerful mix of jazz\, blues\, and R&B. Joyce Grant
  singer/songwriter\, determined at an early age that she was going to be a
  singer and spent her elementary and high school days performing in choir 
 and musical theater. She is the great-great-niece of famed ragtime compose
 r Scott Joplin and has written lyrics to four of his songs. She has partic
 ipated in the West Coast Ragtime Festival for several years. City Swing st
 arted a new chapter in 2007 with jazz singer Joyce Grant. She is the lead 
 vocalist for City Swing\, an 18 piece big band. Grant has been singing jaz
 z in Bay Area venues for over 20 years. A mezzo-soprano with a voice like 
 dark honey\, Grant has a performance resume which includes a wide range of
  venues including the Empire Plush Room and Zingari Ristaurante in San Fra
 ncisco\, the Ledson Hotel in Sonoma\, Sam's Chowder House & Cetrella in Ha
 lf Moon Bay\, the Sticky Rice in Fairfield\, Carneros in Napa\, Slates in 
 Walnut Creek\, Joe's of Lafayette\, and the Woodminster Amphitheater just 
 to name a few. Born in Texarkana\, the town where Scott Joplin was raised\
 , Grant moved to Oakland as a child where she started singing with the Nor
 th Oakland Baptist Church Youth Choir. Since that time she has earned the 
 respect of singers and musicians alike performing professionally in San Fr
 ancisco\, the East Bay\, Walnut Creek\, Napa Valley and beyond. Her unique
  shows consist of a blend of jazz\, blues\, country western\, Rhythm and B
 lues\, and funk. Her vocal interpretations range from sensitive to powerfu
 l to cheeky over a broad spectrum of charts. Joyce Grant is a member of AS
 CAP.
LOCATION:Ferry Taproom
URL:https://www.mareislandbrewingco.com/events/live-music-saturday-0620202
 6
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
