BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Zoe FitzGerald Carter
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T193000
UID:260415bdcaOuwQiUCeeCRdmWJFow
DESCRIPTION:$25 General Admission Doors at 7:30pm. Show from 8:15-10:30pm 
 with one intermission Earlybirds! $3 off each ticket when you use the code
  earlybird21 at checkout. Offer ends june 14th. Promo Codes are not applic
 able at the door. Codes are not case sensitive\, but must be typed as one 
 word. The Real Sarahs are a rising force in the West Coast Americana scene
 \, renowned for their skillful harmonies\, heartfelt songwriting\, and evo
 cative storytelling. Core players Sarah Larkin\, Sarah Ryan\, and Jen Rund
  have captivated audiences with their unique blend of folk\, jazz\, blues\
 , bluegrass\, and country influences. Their organic sound enchants and upl
 ifts\, drawing listeners into the emotional landscapes of their music. The
  Real Sarahs first captured their original songs on their self-titled EP i
 n 2013. Since then\, they have released three subsequent albums showcasing
  their evolving sound\, emotional honesty\, and musical versatility. Their
  songs draw from personal experiences\, life’s triumphs and challenges\,
  and the beauty of human connection. A hallmark of The Real Sarahs is thei
 r live performance chemistry. Their shows blend humor\, storytelling\, and
  intimate musical moments\, creating an atmosphere where audiences feel pe
 rsonally connected to the music. They have shared the stage with numerous 
 folk and Americana artists\, earning a loyal following along the West Coas
 t and beyond. As a trio\, Sarah Ryan\, Sarah Larkin\, and Jen Rund continu
 e to grow creatively and have enjoyed expanding their ensemble to often in
 clude talented instrumental soloists like Candy Girard on fiddle and Emily
  Froberg \\(Charlie Musselwhite\, Eric Lindell\\) on lead guitar\, among o
 thers. Their music entertains and also inspires listeners to embrace vulne
 rability\, empathy\, and the power of storytelling. With their combined ta
 lents\, they represent the heart of modern folk music\, blending tradition
  with personal authenticity. www.therealsarahs.com https://www.instagram.c
 om/the\\_real\\_sarahs www.facebook.com/therealsarahs https://www.youtube.
 com/c/TheRealSarahs https://therealsarahs.bandcamp.com/ Known for her deep
  honey voice and literary lyrics\, award winning Bay Area author turned si
 nger-songwriter\, Zoe FitzGerald Carter\, brings a unique blend of America
 na\, jazz\, blues\, folk and rock. “Zoe sings with personality & self-as
 surance\,” writes John Apice of Americana Highways. "Her tone has author
 ity\, experience & character and she conceives poignant\, well-distinguish
 ed tales with finesse.” The title track of Zoe’s latest album\, Before
  the Machine\, inspired by memories of a pre-smart phone world\, won first
  place in the Corpus Christi Songwriters Contest and the music video premi
 ered on Americana UK and placed in the New Zealand and Vienna film festiva
 ls. Another song from the album\, “Let’s Just Stay Friends\,” was aw
 arded second place from the International Acoustic Music Awards. In additi
 on to writing and performing music\, Zoe teaches memoir and songwriting an
 d has been on the faculty of the Oahu Writers Retreat for the last ten yea
 rs. Her new album\, Chaos By Design\, comes out in the fall of 2026. https
 ://zoecartermusic.com/ https://www.instagram.com/zoe.f.carter/ https://www
 .facebook.com/ZoeFitzgeraldCarterMusic/ https://open.spotify.com/artist/0m
 r5NEf7fLXfvfemenA06e?si=45HnBoB4T\\_OrUfpbXM6Gww&nd=1&dlsi=cf26eb6fada04aa
 9 Recommended If You Like: Indigo Girls\, Bonnie Raitt\, The Wailin' Jenny
 s
LOCATION:The Lost Church
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1474545317605472/?acontext=%7B%22event
 _action_history%22%3A[%7B%22mechanism%22%3A%22lov_feed%22%2C%22surface%22%
 3A%22bookmark%22%7D]%2C%22ref_notif_type%22%3Anull%7D
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
