SUMMARY:The Art of Comics
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T160000
UID:260604eCPGddnqHEaxLDXx9pumCA
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 10\\+\n\nGet ready to unleash your creativity in this fast-paced\
 , idea-packed workshop all about making your own mini-comics. Through fun 
 prompts and simple folding techniques\, you'll learn how to turn a single 
 sheet of paper into a complete comic&mdash\;no experience needed. Explore 
 character creation\, visual storytelling\, and playful experimentation as 
 you sketch\, write\, and assemble your own tiny worlds. Perfect for beginn
 ers and seasoned doodlers alike\, this workshop is all about big ideas in 
 small formats&mdash\;and embracing a little creative chaos along the way.\
 n\nThis workshop is located in the classroom.\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nSa
 rah Maloney \\(they/them\\) is a queer cartoonist and educator whose work 
 has appeared in The Believer\, The Stranger\, the SF Examiner\, Razorcake\
 , Crucial Comix\, and The Rumpus\, alongside over a dozen self-published c
 omics and zines. They hold an MFA in Comics from the California College of
  the Arts and teach workshops for all ages both online and in person. Rece
 nt teaching includes Writing Comics at Portland State University\, a teen 
 summer program at the Sequential Artists Workshop\, and pre-college classe
 s at CCA.\n\nLearn more about Sarah:\n\nwww.maloneydoodles.com\n\n@maloney
 doodles
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-art-of-comics?
 aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
