BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sundays in Sonoma at Viansa Winery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T000000
UID:260324vjiHINh74UmwrBpHMHgFmQ
DESCRIPTION:Viansa Winery feels made for live music\, perched atop the Sum
 mit of Sonoma with sweeping vineyard views and Tuscan-inspired charm. This
  summer and fall\, acclaimed singer-songwriter Greg Lamboy brings his warm
 \, intimate sound to the hilltop terrace for select afternoon performances
  as part of Viansa's outdoor music series. An award-winning guitarist and 
 frontman of the Americana band Pacific Standard\, Lamboy is known for pitc
 h-perfect melodies and deeply personal lyrics. His relaxed\, soulful style
  pairs effortlessly with Viansa's panoramic setting\, estate wines\, and l
 aid-back elegance. Settle in with a tasting\, take in the views\, and enjo
 y an afternoon where strong vocals\, masterful guitar\, and unforgettable 
 songs rise above the everyday. Performance Dates: June 14\, June 21\, July
  12\, July 19\, July 26\, October 4\, and October 18 from 12 pm -3 pm.
LOCATION:Viansa Winery
URL:https://www.sonoma.com/event/sundays-in-sonoma-at-viansa-winery/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Flynn Creek Circus - The Cricket and the Wren
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T200000
UID:260529j-jwPlHp6kOT0oEgAhRwUQ
DESCRIPTION:Flynn Creek Circus Presents ‘The Cricket & the Wren’: a hi
 ghly original\, all-human circus that enchants through breathtaking acroba
 tics and athletically stunning skill. Sponsored by the City of Rohnert Par
 k.\n\nRohnert Park\, CA— June 18 - June 28– This 2026 season\, Flynn C
 reek Circus invites audiences to ‘The Cricket & the Wren’ — memorabl
 e family fun and Artful athleticism under the circus big top.\n\nA merchan
 t’s daughter sets out to find the castle where the horizon meets the sea
 . In order to  break the spell of the Frog Prince\, she must brave a harr
 owing journey filled with wonder.\n\nAlong the adventure\, she encounters 
 Jack and the Beanstalk’s sassy cow\, an out of pocket Pirate and the sec
 ret sacrifice of the cricket and the wren. \n\nFeaturing aerialists\, jug
 glers\, knife throwers\, and laugh out loud comedy\, this circus blends cl
 assic storybook archetypes with imaginative new heroes. The Cricket and th
 e Wren will surprise\, dazzle and delight all ages. \n\nIn addition to th
 e family friendly showings\,  and the interactive children's camp program
  held under the circus big top\,  Flynn Creek Circus also presents the wi
 ldly popular 'Adults Only Show' boasting outrageous acts\, dark comedy\, a
 nd an infamous party atmosphere. Check the website for select adults only 
 showtimes as well as special discount nights.\n\nSpectators for all showin
 gs are invited to the tent to experience the magic up to 30 minutes before
  each show. The event will offer beer\, wine\, and light concession for pu
 rchase and include a 15 minute intermission during the two hour show.\n\nL
 imited free parking is available at 500 City Center Drive. Patrons should 
 then cross the street in the pedestrian crossing at the Rohnert Park Expre
 ssway and State Farm Drive traffic signal.\n\nTickets for Flynn Creek Circ
 us are now available for purchase online at flynncreekcircus.com. Individu
 al ticket prices start at $27 or\, for table reservations\, options start 
 at $98 for two attendees. \n\nFind showtimes and more details on the camp
  programs for ages 5-8 and 7-15 at flynncreekcircus.com\n\nEarly booking i
 s encouraged for this highly anticipated event. \n\nLocation: SE corner l
 ot at Rohnert Park Expressway and State Farm Dr. Rohnert Park\, CA 94928 U
 nder the circus big top\n\nFor more information\, press inquiries\, or int
 erview requests\, please contact Stella Perry at marketing@flynncreekcircu
 s.com. High-resolution images and media resources are also available upon 
 request\n\nAbout Flynn Creek Circus:Flynn Creek Circus is an original\, mo
 dern circus company touring across the Pacific Northwest\, delighting audi
 ences with world-class acrobatics\, storytelling\, and comedy. Known for i
 ts innovative productions and intimate tent shows\, the company redefines 
 the traditional circus experience
LOCATION:Under the circus big top
URL:https://flynncreekcircus.ticketspice.com/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Summertime Livin' Easy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T180000
UID:260519YSmrcvMpVEa3MKm4lDJRtg
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  5/15/26\n\n**JUNE EXHIBIT: SUMME
 RTIME LIVIN’ EASY**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  **June 1 – June 28\, 2026**\n\
 n**RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, June 6\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Nancy Gra
 y  and Gallery artists\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show a
 nd the Gallery’s 29th anniversary.  Be sure to take part in the Gallery
 ’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work by a Gallery artist.  Re
 freshments will feature the Gallery’s signature mocktail: Brushstroke Fi
 zz.**\n\nSonoma County artist\, **Nancy Gray\,** unveils new summer-inspir
 ed acrylic paintings that are a colorful expressive interpretation of the 
 region’s beauty.  Summer is the artist’s favorite season and it shows
 . Drawing inspiration from the French Fauvist tradition\, these works abou
 nd with interpretive color choices and bold brush work.  Non-literal colo
 r expression plays out in “Evening Shade” as backlit trees cast blue t
 endrils of shade dancing on a bed of reddish ground.  Sprinkled across a 
 carpet of golden yellow\, vibrant red poppies glow in “Sundrenched Splen
 dor\,”amplifying the heat of the midday sun.  Red poppies take on a dra
 matic contrasting role in “Lavender Fields Forever” as they play again
 st the purplish blues and lavenders of the fields and sky.  Inspired by t
 he landscape\, these works reinterpret it through emotion and memory.  
 “We are blessed to live amongst Sonoma’s breathtaking scenery – ever
 ywhere I look\, I see a painting\,” noted Gray.\n\nGray has had a lifelo
 ng passion for art.  A Texas native\, she loves living in wine country wi
 th its inspirational landscapes.  Along with the Fauvist painters\, early
  years vacationing on the Caribbean Coast and Belize influenced her bright
  color palette.  She began exhibiting her art in Houston in the early 90
 ’s and continued to focus on her painting after moving to Sonoma County.
   Gray exhibits regionally and has been a member of the Upstairs Art Gall
 ery for five years.\n\nMeet the artist: Gray will host the Gallery on June
  18 and 25 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features
  **Collective Expressions: 29 Years\,** a members’ collaborative show ce
 lebrating the Gallery’s 29th anniversary. Gallery artists offer an excit
 ing mix of mediums\, subject matter and styles emblematic of the Gallery
 ’s dynamic diversity.  Landscapes by Barretta\, Laland\, and Zorich hig
 hlight our region’s beauty\; travel afar with Bird’s Paris cityscape\;
  from sunflowers to roses\, flowers star in works by Gray\, Haley\, Miller
 \, Schaffer\, Sumner and Wilson\; succulent oranges are the focus of Stolp
 er’s stunning still-life\; lovable pets are the subject of Tobin-Charles
 ton’s jewelry\; abstracts by Morgan and Reid bring a moving contemporary
  complement\; figurative works by Rapp\, Roney and Shore round out this cl
 assic to contemporary overview of the Upstairs artistic family.\n\nAlso jo
 in us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, June 4\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART 
 NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community ev
 ent celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participating. 
  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Hea
 ldsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **ww
 w.upstairsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly 
 Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Superhero Camp
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T143000
UID:2605142l3mev_XlUG34sUfOASucw
DESCRIPTION:Make the most of summer with award-winning Gymnastics Camps at
  SGA! Keep children’s bodies and brains active with careful guidance fro
 m our trained instructors\, and have some fun\, too. We’ll play in our o
 utdoor inflatable water parks\, eat lunch in the park\, and learn basic gy
 mnastics techniques every day from 8:30 AM - 2:30 PM. Each week has its ow
 n unique theme with specialized crafts\, games\, activities\, and learning
 . Enroll in one week\, a few\, or all ten! Sign up on our site\, email us\
 , or call us to register. Spots are limited.\n\n-This week’s theme is: S
 UPERHEROES-\n\nBecome a superhero for the week at camp! Dive into a week o
 f high-flying gymnastics\, superhero training\, games\, obstacle courses\,
  and play! This camp is perfect for burning that summer energy\, while als
 o building strength so your child can become the hero they were born to be
 !\n\nCamps are best suited for children ages 4 to 12. All participants mus
 t be fully toilet-trained.\n\nStudents should wear a t-shirt with elastic 
 waistband shorts/pants\, or a leotard. Long hair must be pulled back. No j
 ewelry\, jeans\, dresses\, or skirts. Please wear or pack clothing layers 
 for if the weather permits us to adventure outside!\n\nPlease pack your ch
 ild\\(ren\\) a PEANUT-FREE lunch\, water bottle\, and comfortable shoes. M
 orning snacks will be provided.
LOCATION:Sonoma Gymnastics Academy
URL:https://sonomagymnasticsacademy.com/camps/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wine Tails Trail at Cuvaison Winery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T170000
UID:2605084trYu_lAGUa2JHgsXNTnlg
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a new way to experience Cuvaison with your canine compan
 ion on the Wine Tails Trail. This self-guided vineyard walk winds just und
 er a mile through our Los Carneros estate\, with QR code stops highlightin
 g the history of our vines and winemaking. Guests begin their adventure by
  checking in with our Concierge for a map and orientation before setting o
 ff on the trail.\n\nAfter the walk\, return to the estate and enjoy a seat
 ed tasting of our current release wines\, while your pup relaxes by your s
 ide and enjoys a selection of “Barkuterie.” The Wine Tails Trail is a 
 chance to stretch your legs\, explore the vineyard\, and savor Cuvaison in
  the company of your best friend.\n\nWhen booking this experience\, please
  plan for the dog walk to begin at the time you select. The walk itself av
 erages about 45 minutes\, though you’ll also check in with our Concierge
