BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sculpture Uncovered: A Survey of Materials & Methods
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T200000
UID:260604xDOWxD6tz0ik6wpHH3xTLw
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 13 and over\n\nAbout this Class:\n\nThis presentation offers a su
 rvey of sculptural practice across a range of materials and techniques. Fr
 om traditional processes like carving and casting to contemporary approach
 es using mixed media and found objects\, the talk explores how artists thi
 nk in three dimensions and bring form to life. Through visual examples and
  clear explanations\, participants will gain insight into the possibilitie
 s of sculpture and the diverse ways artists approach making. Ideal for any
 one curious about the language of form\, material\, and space.\n\nThis cla
 ss is located in the Main Gallery.\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nMarty Marfin 
 is a Sonoma County&ndash\;based maker\, educator\, and fabricator with ext
 ensive experience across education\, media\, and museum production. He cur
 rently serves as Innovative Arts Makerspace Manager at the Academy of Inno
 vative Arts in Forestville and as Community Engagement Representative and 
 grant writer at Chimera Arts. His past roles include Maker Media Lab Manag
 er at Maker Media and Model Making Studio Manager at the California Colleg
 e of the Arts\, where he supported thousands of student projects. With a b
 ackground spanning sculpture\, prototyping\, and exhibit design\, Marty ha
 s created immersive museum installations for institutions including the Am
 erican Museum of Natural History and the Field Museum.\n\nLearn more about
  Marty! \n\nwww.martymarfin.com
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pacacademy-sculpture-surve
 y?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Draw What You See With the iPad
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T160000
UID:260604iciKpnjlUU-0pYiB05mbKA
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 13\\+\n\nThis class offers a practical\, in-depth exploration of 
 Procreate on the iPad\, helping you grow both artistically and technically
 . Guided by Jeremy's methodical approach&mdash\;shaped by decades as a pro
 fessional artist&mdash\;you'll learn essential tools and workflows\, from 
 setting up your canvas and customizing brushes to managing layers\, color\
 , references\, and exporting your work. Alongside technical skills\, the c
 ourse emphasizes drawing what you see\, teaching you to compose effectivel
 y\, simplify subjects into shapes and tones\, build from general to detail
 ed\, and create strong focal points. The goal is to equip you with techniq
 ues that support confident mark-making and allow your unique artistic voic
 e to emerge naturally.\n\nThis workshop is located in the classroom. \n\nA
 bout the Teacher: \n\nJeremy Sutton  is a digital artist and educator whos
 e lifelong passion for drawing evolved from studies in physics at Oxford&m
 dash\;where he also trained in fine art&mdash\;through further art study i
 n The Hague\, to a career at the forefront of digital painting. After movi
 ng to Silicon Valley in 1988 and embracing digital tools in the early 1990
 s\, he became a full-time artist known for vibrant\, color-rich work inspi
 red by artists like Claude Monet and Henri Matisse. Sutton is internationa
 lly recognized for live event painting at corporate\, cultural\, and museu
 m venues\, including collaborations with Cirque du Soleil\, appearances at
  the de Young Museum and the Smithsonian American Art Museum\, and perform
 ances with jazz musicians. Founder of PaintboxTV\, he is also a dedicated 
 teacher\, sharing his process through books\, tutorials\, and workshops wo
 rldwide\, and is based in San Francisco.\n\nLearn more about Jeremy: \n\nj
 eremysutton.com\n\n@jeremydsutton
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-draw-with-ipad
 ?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wing It! Painting Butterflies & Moths in Watercolor
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T120000
UID:260604PUQs7ZIxoUmz5oa7hpmHTA
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 18\\+\n\nAlways wanted to try watercolor painting? Join Sally-Ann
  Langley for a fun-filled foray into the world of whimsical botanicals and
  moths. Painting in a free and joyful style\, you'll use simple shapes and
  lush color\, finishing out with botanical embellishments. The style will 
 be relaxed and playful\, with demonstrations on watercolor techniques incl
 uding washes\, blending\, layering and texture. This is a great class for 
 beginners and for more experienced artists who are interested in learning 
 a new technique.\n\nThis workshop is located in the classroom.\n\nAbout th
 e Teacher: \n\nSally-Ann Langley is a Northern California multidisciplinar
 y artist based in Petaluma\, CA. Sally-Ann received her BA in Graphic Desi
 gn from Newport College of Art in the UK. After 20 years as a packaging de
 signer\, she now works as a freelance illustrator and licensed artist sell
 ing her work online and on products nationwide. Sally-Ann has taught works
 hops in Morocco\, Sonoma and Petaluma.\n\nLearn more about Sally-Ann: \n\n
 www.slangleyart.com\n\n@sally\\_ann\\_langley
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-butterflies-an
 d-moths?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Drawing The Figure
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T210000
UID:260604Hlf0ZvdiHkmT1q8L8Pitpg
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 18\\+\n\nWelcome to life drawing&mdash\;where humans refuse to ho
 ld still just long enough to make things interesting. In this relaxed and 
 good-humored class\, you'll learn how to capture gesture\, proportion\, an
 d structure without overthinking every line. We'll practice quick poses\, 
 longer studies\, and the fine art of not panicking when the pose changes r
 ight as you finally &ldquo\;get it.&rdquo\; Along the way\, you'll sharpen
  your observation skills\, loosen up your drawing style\, and gain confide
 nce in capturing the human form as it really is&mdash\;beautiful\, complex
 \, and occasionally a bit wobbly on paper. All levels welcome\, including 
 brave beginners and seasoned artists ready to laugh at their own drawings.
 \n\nStudents bring: Favorite drawing pad and pencils\n\nThis workshop is l
 ocated in the classroom. \n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nCharles &ldquo\;Chuck&
 rdquo\; is a lifelong artist and painter-illustrator whose career spans ba
 ck to 1976\, known for storytelling work that blends humor and drama while
  delighting clients and collectors. He received the Distinguished Educator
  in the Arts Award from the Society of Illustrators and an honorary doctor
 ate from the Academy of Art University\, where he served for many years as
  Chair of the School of Illustration before retiring in 2021. He is also a
  founding artist member of the Sonoma and Telluride Plein Air groups and h
 as exhibited widely.\n\nTo learn more about Charles:\n\ncharlespyle.net\n\
 n@chuckpyle
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pacacademy-drawing-the-fig
 ure?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Art of Letting Go: Intuitive Ink Painting & the Zen Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260622T160000
UID:2606042bTnL_0SPUuyvr7WRTTxDA
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 18\\+\n\nStep into a calming\, immersive workshop where intuition
  guides the brush and imperfection becomes a source of beauty. Blending Ea
 stern and Western approaches to abstraction\, this experience weaves toget
 her meditation\, movement\, and expressive mark-making to create deeply pe
 rsonal paintings. Rooted in the Japanese aesthetic of wabi-sabi\, particip
 ants release the need for perfection and explore the unexpected through in
 k\, watercolor\, and gesture. The session begins with gentle centering\, t
 hen moves into practices like painting the ensō&mdash\;the Zen circle sym
 bolizing presence and wholeness&mdash\;using Asian brushes and layered tec
 hniques to build atmosphere\, depth\, and emotion. No prior experience is 
 needed&mdash\;just a willingness to slow down\, connect\, and create from 
 within.\n\nThis workshop is located in the classroom.\n\nAbout the Teacher
 : \n\nSherrie Lovler holds a B.A. in Studio Art and has taught calligraphy
  and related arts for decades at institutions including Ghost Ranch\, La R
 omita School of Art in Italy\, Northern Arizona University\, and major cal
 ligraphy guilds and conferences. She is the author\, illustrator\, and des
 igner of On Softer Ground\, an IPPY gold medal winner for book design\, an
 d her latest book\,Distant Voices\, explores art as a collaboration with n
 ature\, memory\, and unseen influences. She is an Art at the Source and Ar
 t Trails artist and recently had a solo exhibit at Gallery Route One in Po
 int Reyes Station.
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-intuitive-ink-
 painting?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
