UID:26060412U7ayUuZk6RvziFvU76gA
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 13 and over\n\nAbout this Class:\n\nCurious about digital art but
  not sure where to begin? This hands-on workshop is designed for tradition
 al artists ready to expand their creative practice into the digital realm.
  You'll learn how to choose the right tools&mdash\;tablets\, apps\, and so
 ftware&mdash\;while exploring essential techniques like working with layer
 s\, brushes\, and digital color. The class also covers how to combine scan
 ned drawings with digital painting and prepare your artwork for high-quali
 ty prints. With a focus on experimentation and practical skills\, this wor
 kshop makes digital tools approachable\, intuitive\, and directly relevant
  to your existing artistic process.\n\nThis class is on ZOOM. You will rec
 eive a zoom link a few days before class.\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nPryce 
 Jones is an artist\, designer\, and educator whose work explores how peopl
 e experience stories across digital\, physical\, and interactive environme
 nts. With a background in architecture\, video games\, and immersive media
 \, he began his career at Gensler before spending nearly two decades as an
  environment artist and art director with studios including LucasArts\, Ei
 dos\, Activision\, and Gazillion Entertainment. His current practice bridg
 es fine art\, creative placemaking\, and emerging technologies to engage c
 ommunities around history and identity. He has served as founding MFA Dire
 ctor at the Academy of Art University and now teaches Game Arts at the Cal
 ifornia College of the Arts\, mentoring the next generation of artists and
  designers.\n\nLearn more about Pryce: www.prycejonesart.com
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pacacademy-digital-tools-z
 oom?aff=cityspark
