DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nWednesdays Weekly · 8 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nJun
 e 10 – July 29\, 2026\n\n6:00 PM – 9:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 117\, C
 eramics Studio\n\nCategory\n\nCeramics\, Extended Classes\n\nExperience Le
 vel\n\nAdvanced\n\nAges\n\n17\\+\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$265\n\nMaterial
 s Fee:\n\n$30\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$295\n\nprogram overview\n\nT
 his session is designed for people who have already taken multiple wheel t
 hrowing courses. A continuation of our intermediate course\, this upper le
 vel / advanced course will help you hone your throwing skills through more
  complex demos\, and nuanced approaches to technical throwing. In this 8 w
 eek course\, students will dive deep into developing their own unique voic
 e as they build a technical toolset for the independent maker. In addition
  to throwing\, surface decoration techniques will be explored as well as t
 he opportunity to experiment with different clay bodies. With your 8 week 
 class registration\, students receive the opportunity to purchase a studio
  pass for ½ off during the duration of their class. Sign ups for membersh
 ip will be included.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/pottery-on-the-wheel-advanc
 ed/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
